# Animal Shaman

**Alignments.** Any, but the spirits tend to avoid selfish people.

The Animal Shaman draws his powers from the spirits of animals and, though he
takes one species as his own totem, is devoted to all of them - helping and
protecting the Native American people, the spirits and the animals around him.
He can heal animals, cure their diseases and sometimes even call a slain one
back to life.

## Lore

Some settle in villages, but most are wanderers who treat the whole continent
as their domain, riding a regular circuit or travelling everywhere, and staying
long with people and places they like. In the wild they adopt packs and herds
and guard them fiercely - accepting the hunt as part of the Circle of Life, but
taking retribution for slaughter done for sport or trophies. They often join
Totem Warriors against the Man-Monsters.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

Ceremonial garments and a headdress or animal skin, a hooded cloak, moccasins,
a shovel, a hand axe, a tanning frame, 50 feet of rope, a week of dried food, a
mixing bowl, a grinding stone, sewing needles, thread and 1D4 sticks of
charcoal. A bow and arrows and two S.D.C. weapons of choice, typically a spear
and a tomahawk.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'animal-shaman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'animal-shaman';

